From: aiden build <build@aiden.local>
Subject: [PATCH] adb: add boringssl googletest include for gtest_prod.h

libziparchive/zip_writer.h includes <gtest/gtest_prod.h> for the
FRIEND_TEST macro. This header exists in the vendored BoringSSL's
third_party/googletest/include but is not in the default include path,
causing:

  zip_writer.h:22:10: fatal error: gtest/gtest_prod.h: No such file or directory

Add boringssl/third_party/googletest/include to the include paths for
libadb, libadb_crypto_defaults and libadb_tls_connection_defaults.

Aiden-local patch (not from upstream nmeum/android-tools).
---
--- a/vendor/CMakeLists.adb.txt
+++ b/vendor/CMakeLists.adb.txt
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 target_include_directories(libadb PUBLIC
 	base/libs/androidfw/include
 	boringssl/include
+	boringssl/third_party/googletest/include
 	core/adb
 	core/adb/crypto/include
 	core/adb/pairing_auth/include
@@ -66,6 +67,7 @@
 	core/adb
 	core/adb/crypto/include
 	boringssl/include
+	boringssl/third_party/googletest/include
 	core/libcrypto_utils/include
 	libbase/include)
 
@@ -78,6 +80,7 @@
 	core/adb
 	core/adb/tls/include
 	boringssl/include
+	boringssl/third_party/googletest/include
 	libbase/include)
 
 add_library(liblog STATIC
